This is as compiled.
files here:
   maxops/README (this document)
   
   maxops/maxopsperinst.c The source to create the .o
   maxops/maxopsperinst.o (altered to set maximum ops per instruction
    to zero, which is erroneous.)
   maxops/original-maxopsperinst.o (as compiled maximum ops
    per instruction is 1)

The maximum ops per instruction is in .debug_line
which begins at 0x1f7.  The actual maximum ops per instruction
is at byte 0x204.

Do not recompile, please.

cc -c -O0 -gdwarf-5 maxopsperinst.c

Using a dwarfdump which catches the error:
dwarfdump -l -vv maxopsperinst.o

